title: lattice-gated-fetch must not fall through to ordinary fetch after a dock allow
status: closed
priority: P0
track: aep28-library-components
wave: lattice-gated-fetch
plan: none
repo: NLA-AEP-v2.8-open-source
depends_on: none
scope: AEP-Base-Node/crate/src/docking.rs AEP-Components/lattice-gated-fetch/crate AEP-Components/lattice-channels/lib AEP-NOSHIP/AEP-SDKs/typescript AEP-NOSHIP/AEP-SDKs/javascript AEP-NOSHIP/AEP-SDKs/html-css/lattice_client.js AEP-NOSHIP/AEP-SDKs/python/aep-protocol/aep/lattice_client.py AEP-NOSHIP/AEP-SDKs/rust/src/lattice.rs CHANGELOG.md Cargo.toml scripts/gate-aep28-env-061.sh
notes: Closed. After dock allow the kernel executes bound HTTP and returns http. Clients consume dock http. Ordinary fetch after allow is Deny. BIOSECURE UNVACCINATED SUPREME USER APPROVAL for python lattice_client.py so the existing client stops urlopen after dock allow.
acceptance: DockFrameResponse.http carries bound HTTP after LATTICE_GATEWAY_REQUEST allow. lattice-gated-fetch twins do not ordinary-fetch after dock allow. Crate aep-lattice-gated-fetch fails if docking.rs or a twin still falls through. CI gate scripts/gate-aep28-env-061.sh runs cargo test --lib and cargo run.
